# The committed gnav bundle is a generated artifact, so a textual merge of it
# is meaningless — the source tree is the source of truth. To stop it from
# ever blocking a merge (the queue merges server-side, where custom drivers
# don't run), we merge it with git's BUILT-IN `union` driver: on an
# overlapping change, keep BOTH sides instead of raising a conflict.
#
# The union'd result is momentarily invalid, but the `rebuild-dist` workflow
# regenerates the correct bundle on the next push to stage/main, so the
# union'd state never survives. (union is built into git — no config needed,
# and GitHub honors it, unlike config-defined drivers such as `ours`.)
#
#   merge=union → never conflict; keep both sides on an overlapping region.
#   -diff       → don't render textual diffs for these minified blobs.
federal/libs/global-navigation/dist/main.js     merge=union -diff
federal/libs/global-navigation/dist/main.js.map merge=union -diff
